## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical understanding of ephemeral cross‑account access, least privilege, VPC endpoints, and auditability. It also probes revocation semantics for temporary credentials.

## Key Concepts
- STS AssumeRole with session duration
- Cross‑account IAM roles and trust policies
- S3 bucket policies with resource and condition constraints
- VPC Endpoint restrictions
- CloudTrail auditing
- Revocation mechanics for temporary credentials

## Code Example
```javascript
// trust policy example (role in data owner account)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_AWS_ACCOUNT:role/PartnerDataAccess"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "data-exchange-2026"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// bucket policy snippet (only for the assumed role and specific VPC endpoint)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::PARTNER_AWS_ACCOUNT:role/PartnerDataAccess"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::partner-data-bucket",
        "arn:aws:s3:::partner-data-bucket/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceVpce": "vpce-EXAMPLE"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement revocation within 60 seconds?
- What are trade-offs between VPC Endpoint and public access in this scenario?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-account log delivery, least privilege, and lifecycle handling in a real SaaS pattern.

## Key Concepts
- Cross-account IAM roles and bucket policies
- TLS-only S3 access and private endpoints
- CMK encryption and CloudTrail validation
- Onboarding/offboarding automation and rollback

## Code Example
```json
// Central bucket policy sketch
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::<central-id>:role/TenantLogPublisher"},
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::central-logs-bucket/tenant-prefix/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "true"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
// Trust policy sketch for TenantLogPublisher (in central/account_root)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"Service": "delivery.logs.amazonaws.com"},
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:SourceAccount": "<central-id>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test end-to-end log delivery across accounts?
- How would you handle rotation of the CMK and rotation of the tenant role?
